                <div class="experience-section">
                    <h3>Education</h3>
                    <div class="experience-item">
                        <h4>Master of Science in Management</h4>
                        <p class="experience-period">University of Illinois <span aria-hidden="true">•</span> Expected 2027</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="experience-item">
                        <h4>Bachelor of Science in Computer Science</h4>
                        <p class="experience-period">Aurora University <span aria-hidden="true">•</span> December 2019</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="experience-section">
                <h3>Professional Journey</h3>
                <p class="experience-intro">Backend software engineer building production fintech systems and shared AI/LLM infrastructure. Experience spans Python APIs, financial integrations, applied AI, and cross-team platform leadership.</p>

                <div class="experience-item">
                    <h4>Backend Software Engineer</h4>
                    <p class="experience-period">Halo Investing Inc. <span aria-hidden="true">•</span> Nov 2025 – Present</p>
                    <div class="experience-areas">
                        <div class="experience-area">
                            <h5>Backend &amp; Fintech Engineering</h5>
                            <p class="experience-description">Python APIs and data models for trade-level billing, plus Pershing and Goldman Sachs trading and custody integration components. Role-based analytics APIs feed the product views where issuers benchmark their auctions against anonymized market data.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="experience-area">
                            <h5>Applied AI Products</h5>
                            <p class="experience-description">Three production AI features spanning LLM-based financial analysis, RAG and vector retrieval, Model Context Protocol, conversational interfaces, and document processing.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="experience-area">
                            <h5>Shared AI/LLM Platform</h5>
                            <p class="experience-description">I built and operate self-hosted LiteLLM and Langfuse, giving 4+ teams one instrumented path to models: routing, prompt management, caching, and observability. I retrofitted another team's document-processing service onto it, and advise roughly 12 engineering and product stakeholders on architecture, provider selection, reliability, and safety.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="experience-pair">
                    <div class="experience-item">
                        <h4>Software Developer</h4>
                        <p class="experience-period">OSM Worldwide <span aria-hidden="true">•</span> Nov 2023 – Aug 2025</p>
                        <p class="experience-description">Built C#/.NET applications for the carrier-routing and shipping-label workflows behind USPS and OnTrac operations, tuned the SQL Server schemas and stored procedures underneath them, and led the move toward AWS Lambda. WinForms tooling and workflow redesigns saved more than 20 staff-hours a week.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="experience-item">
                        <h4>Customer Excellence Engineer</h4>
                        <p class="experience-period">Integral Ad Science <span aria-hidden="true">•</span> 2020 – 2023</p>
                        <p class="experience-description">The go-to person for complex data problems: automated 1,200+ recurring SQL reports, built 20+ Looker models and dashboards for 50+ stakeholders, and ran discrepancy, data-quality, and fraud investigations in Snowflake and AWS Athena.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="download-section">
                <a href="/AustinOrphanResume.pdf" download class="download-resume">
                    <i class="ph-duotone ph-download"></i>
                    Download Resume
